A||||6||Shiner||Best way to remove rocker panel rivets?||||5||
Z||000000||Shiner||10-27-2000||06:16 PM||||I have to get the driver's side rocker panel off the SE (aero), so that it can be placed on my GT.  Now, the GT had a coupe rocker panel on it, which was pretty trashed, so we experimented on it.  Well, we couldn't find a good way to get those wack-assed rivets out without damaging the rocker somewhat.  I am not sure if these things are stock pieces.  They are what looks and feels like aluminum with a VERY hard core (which was a beotch to drill through).  On the other side, they are kind of like a flower.  They are completely mushroomed there, and are really no fun to deal with.<P> So, the question is, are these stock rivets?  And what is the best way to take these off?  Thanks in advance!<P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||10-27-2000||06:29 PM||||Take a center punch and knock out the center of rivit. Take a drill with a 3/8th or so bit and drill the rivit head off. If it begins to rotate, ****  the drill slightly so it still cuts.<P>OK, it didn't like that word!<BR>Tilt the drill slightly....<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 10-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||10-27-2000||06:59 PM||||I use an impact hammer and a flat blade chisel. Piece-O-Cake.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||4
Z||000003||bHooper||10-27-2000||09:16 PM||||Yes those are stock rivits, and yes they are difficult to remove.<P>Drill em out, then use the punch... or stick a phillips head screw driver threw it, wiggle it around some and they should come right out!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_Freak||10-28-2000||12:14 AM||||What do you use to put the rocker back on?  Is there a special tool.  I'm wanting to take the whole body off my second GT to paint it and then put it on my running one.  Any help is appreciated||||reg||1
Z||000005||tgowens||10-28-2000||12:52 AM||||don't forget to use a metric hammer and metric punch to get those rivits out!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/tgowens_sig.gif">                          <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> - Blue '87 GT - Gold '87 GT<BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog.org" TARGET=_blank>www.cfog.org</A> - Classic Fiero Owners Group||||reg||1
Z||000006||bHooper||10-28-2000||08:14 AM||||thats right, tgownes, or the body want line up correctly!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>seriously, you can purchase those rivits from the fiero store, or buy standard rivits from a hardware vendor.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
